      "text": "To find the length of the tunnel, we need to determine the distance traveled by the front of the train while the tail of the train is exiting the tunnel.\n\nFirst, let's convert the time from minutes to hours:\n3 minutes = 3/60 hours = 1/20 hours\n\nNext, let's calculate the distance traveled by the front of the train in this time period:\nDistance = Speed * Time\nDistance = 60 mph * (1/20) hr = 3 miles\n\nThis means that the front of the train traveled 3 miles into the tunnel. To find the length of the tunnel, we add the initial length of the train to the distance the front of the train traveled inside the tunnel:\nLength of tunnel = Length of train + Distance traveled inside tunnel\nLength of tunnel = 1 mile + 3 miles = 4 miles\n\nTherefore, the length of the tunnel is 4 miles.",
